.TH SWAYDESK-DESKTOP-CONFIG 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.2" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-desktop\-config \- read the desktop configuration and apply the accent color
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
get KEY
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
generate
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
apply
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
css
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
setup
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
enabled NAME
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
waybar
[TEMPLATE]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml for the shell scripts and writes the files that depend on the accent color.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-desktop\-config (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-desktop\-config); the process name is sway\-desktop\-config too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B get KEY
Print a value of the configuration; an unknown key exits 2.
.TP
.B generate
Write the files that depend on the color.
.TP
.B apply
Write the files and reload Sway.
.TP
.B css
Print the accent colors as GTK CSS (@define\-color).
.TP
.B setup
The first login in the packaged session: copy from the skeleton what is missing in the home folder, then generate.
.TP
.B enabled NAME
Exit 0 if the component NAME is on in the [enabled] table of the configuration, 1 if it is off. NAME is a key of
[enabled], such as dock, or of [enabled.bar] with the bar. prefix, such as bar.weather. A key that is absent is
on; an unknown NAME prints a warning and counts as on. The session's sway\-if\-enabled helper uses it to skip the
components that are off.
.TP
.B waybar [TEMPLATE]
Write ~/.config/swaydesk\-desktop/waybar/config.jsonc: the Waybar configuration TEMPLATE (by default the
package's in the packaged session, ~/.config/waybar/config.jsonc otherwise) without the modules turned off in
[enabled.bar], and print its path. The session's sway\-waybar runs it before each start and falls back to the
template when it fails. generate writes it too.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language (locale), accent color (accent), GTK and icon themes (gtk_theme, icon_theme), folder color (folder_color), file manager (file_manager), weather location (weather_location) and holidays (holidays). The fonts come from the GTK system font.
.IP
The [enabled] table turns session components off with false: dock, app_grid, switcher, notifications, osd,
clipboard_history, nightlight, bing_wallpaper, polkit_agent, update_notifier and displays (the automatic
screen profiles and the rescue that turns the screens on when none is on; the Displays app stays). The [enabled.bar] table does
the same for the Waybar modules: weather, clock, media, recording, notifications, clipboard, language, system,
brightness, caffeine, bluetooth, network, volume, battery and power. A key that is absent is on. A change takes
effect at the next login; for the bar, also when Waybar restarts.
.IP
The shortcuts key picks the keyboard shortcut profile: swaydesk (the default), i3, hyprland, niri or dwm. generate
writes ~/.config/sway/config.d/00-keys.conf, which includes the keys of every profile (keys/base.conf) and then the
profile's own file (keys/<profile>.conf, in /usr/share/swaydesk\-desktop/sway/keys for the package session).
Run swaymsg reload after generate, or change the profile in the help window (Super+F1). The dwm profile uses Alt
as the modifier, as dwm does. The user's ~/.config/sway/config.d/50-local.conf is read after any profile and
wins over it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/config.d/00\-keys.conf
The includes of the shortcut profile, written by generate.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk\-desktop/waybar/config.jsonc
The Waybar configuration without the modules turned off, written by waybar and generate.
.TP
.I /usr/share/swaydesk\-desktop/skel/
The skeleton that setup copies.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-theme (1)
